        "pitch_deg_gallery": {
          "range": [
            20,
            30
          ],
          "unit": "deg",
          "kind": "measured"
        }
      },
      "rule": "Steep hipped or double-pitched roof, 40-50 degrees on the main mass, breaking to 20-30 degrees over the gallery at the wall plane (c03, hard); a single continuous slope is a later Anglo simplification.",
      "note": "Overrides the inherited mediterranean-vernacular low pitch (3:12-6:12, roughly 14-27 degrees), which is a dry-climate answer; the Gulf Coast's heavy rainfall wants a fast-shedding steep roof instead, and the pitch break itself is the tradition's single fastest diagnostic tell.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "status": "drafted"
